# [item 3 / GPU render] the runtime env that makes the stewie-gazebo image render on the NVIDIA GPU instead
# of software mesa. Requires Aaron's docker features.cdi=true (2026-07-04) so `--device nvidia.com/gpu=all`
# mounts the nvidia GL userspace at /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/nvidia/current.
#
# TWO things were needed (both discovered 2026-07-04):
#  1. LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=0 (the image bakes =1, correct for CPU-only CI; it forces software GL and fights
#     the mounted nvidia GL). Override to 0 when a GPU is present.
#  2. The launch must NOT pass `--headless-rendering` (EGL) -- that path cannot obtain a GL 3.3 context and
#     crashed OGRE2 at render-window init. Render via GLX on the X display (run under xvfb-run); that path gets
#     GL 3.3 from the nvidia driver (GPU) or llvmpipe (CPU). Fixed in gz_sim.launch.py 2026-07-04.
#
# Put the nvidia GL libs on the loader with LDCONFIG, NOT LD_LIBRARY_PATH (which would shadow the ROS2/gz libs
# and break the launch): inside the container run
#     echo /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/nvidia/current > /etc/ld.so.conf.d/nvidia.conf && ldconfig
# then `xvfb-run -a ros2 launch stewie_bringup gz_sim.launch.py` renders cameras + points on the GPU.
#
# Usage:  docker run --rm --device nvidia.com/gpu=all --env-file deploy/ros2/render_gpu.env stewie-gazebo:jazzy \
#           bash -lc 'echo /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/nvidia/current >/etc/ld.so.conf.d/nvidia.conf; ldconfig; \
#             source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash; source install/setup.bash; \
#             xvfb-run -a ros2 launch stewie_bringup gz_sim.launch.py'
NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES=all
LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=0
__GLX_VENDOR_LIBRARY_NAME=nvidia
